    "**Example.** $g(x) = \\cos x$ has one fixed point $x_\\ast \\approx 0.739$. Since $g'(x) = -\\sin x$, we get $|g'(x_\\ast)| = \\sin(0.739) \\approx 0.67 < 1$: it attracts, and the error shrinks by about $0.67$ per step.\n",
    "\n",
    "$g(x) = x^2$ has two fixed points ($x_\\ast^2 = x_\\ast$, so $x_\\ast = 0$ or $1$). With $g'(x) = 2x$: $g'(0) = 0$ attracts, $g'(1) = 2$ repels."
   ]
